WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.840
tomorrow, Joe Biden will be president of the
United States.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.749
We're sort of closing the book on the Trump
presidency today in a few different ways.

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:08.940
And one such way is looking at approval rating.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.670
Donald Trump is leaving the White House with
the lowest job approval of his presidency,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.590
which is 29 percent.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.950
And yet it still seems so high.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.870
How could nearly a third of the people in
this country, less than a third, but nearly

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:28.030
a third of the people in this country think
he's doing a good job?

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:33.300
Still, he's been doing nothing for months
other than inciting that riotous insurrection

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.300
on January 6th.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:43.219
And it is true that Trump voters have grown
more critical of Trump in his post-election

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:44.219
conduct.

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:50.390
The share of Trump supporters who describe
his conduct as poor has doubled over the last

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.739
two months from 10 percent to 20 percent.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:59.480
A significant majority of Americans don't
want Trump Trump to remain a major political

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.620
figure after he leaves office.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:07.810
About two thirds say Trump should be should
evaporate as a as a primary political figure

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:09.539
of the United States.

00:01:09.539 --> 00:01:15.409
Joe Biden is entering with 64 percent positive
opinion, which is great only in the sense

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:21.500
that it bodes well and sets Biden up well
for the crucial start of his presidency, where

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.590
we need everybody on the same page in order
to finally get this pandemic under control,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.159
scale up vaccination and do the things that
have to be done.

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:31.759
So those are all good signs.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:38.189
But in term of the terms of the January 6th
Trump riots, three quarters of the public

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:45.259
say that Trump bears at least some responsibility
for the violence and destruction committed

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:47.049
by some of his supporters.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:53.759
52 percent say Trump bears a lot of responsibility,
but we still have twenty four percent.

00:01:53.759 --> 00:02:01.409
Nearly a quarter of this country says Trump
has zero responsibility for what took place.

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:05.299
That's extraordinarily weaponized disinformation.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:12.720
And then maybe most disturbing, a majority
of Republicans still think that Donald Trump

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.140
actually won the election.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:22.550
Understand that 64 percent of Republican voters
still believe as of a few days ago when this

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.260
survey was done, that it is actually Donald
Trump who won the election.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:33.840
Two thirds of Republicans believe the guy
who's being sworn in tomorrow did not really

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.840
win.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.380
And by the way, six percent of Democrats also
believe Trump won.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.540
I'd be interested in talking to some of those
folks that that's that's quite a bit that's

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.830
just as depressing, quite frankly.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:50.480
Meanwhile, this is not the only data point
from Pew in the Gallup presidential approval

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.880
tracking poll.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.560
Trump also falling there to a presidency low
of 34 percent approval.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.450
And I have the same reaction to both the 29
percent and 34 percent approval numbers, 29

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.200
percent and 34 percent approval for Trump
are way too high.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.320
Those numbers tell us that something is very
wrong with the country, as if we didn't already

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.320
know.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.320
But it confirms it.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.950
Approval should be zero if only all of this
had been completely predictable when Donald

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.090
Trump ran for president back in 2015.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.070
Oh, wait a second.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:27.120
It was completely predictable and we were
predicting that it would be this bad.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:34.400
So there will be time for postmortems, but
it's still shocking and saddening that there

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:42.070
are people who thought Hillary would be the
same as Trump or Hillary would be as bad as

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:47.640
Trump, or it would make no difference to to
the day to day, day to day lives of Americans,

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.920
whether it's Trump or Hillary.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.780
Some people over the last year were saying
similar things about Joe Biden.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.100
Joe Biden would be as bad as Trump.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.580
I hope no one is listening to those people
anymore because they've given up their right

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:01.930
to be listened to.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.220
I'm not saying they shouldn't be allowed to
speak.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.080
I'm not violating anyone's suggesting anyone's
First Amendment rights be violated.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.190
I'm just saying at this point, we have enough
evidence to realize we shouldn't be listening

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.650
to those people.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:20.840
By the way, there are also people who went
from voting for Bernie to voting for Trump

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.880
that also knowing everything we know now is
extraordinarily disturbing.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.130
It was disturbing back in 2016.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:32.160
It's even more disturbing now because everything
has been so utterly predictable and yet some

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.890
people are still acting surprised.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.250
So good news.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.490
Trump's going out with the lowest approval
rating of his presidency.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:44.130
Bad news, nearly a third of the country, nearly
a third of the country, meaning about 70 million

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:49.880
people still support the absolutely.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:54.030
I'm sorry, no doubt 90 something million people.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.660
My math was wrong.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.720
Something around 90 million people still think
Trump is doing a good job, and that's going

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.410
to be something we'll have to deal with for
much, much more time than Trump is in office,

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:32.220
which is fortunately just a few more hours.

